    "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are a helpful assistant.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nAdam rolled two standard six-sided dice once.  What is the probability that he did not roll a prime number on either die? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n\nThink step by step inside <think> </think> tags, then give your final answer inside \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nTo determine the probability that Adam did not roll a prime number on either die, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the prime numbers on a six-sided die:**\n   The prime numbers between 1 and 6 are 2, 3, and 5.\n\n2. **Identify the non-prime numbers on a six-sided die:**\n   The non-prime numbers between 1 and 6 are 1, 4, and 6.\n\n3. **Calculate the probability of not rolling a prime number on a single die:**\n   There are 3 non-prime numbers out of 6 possible outcomes on a single die.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability of not rolling a prime number on one die} = \\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the probability of not rolling a prime number on both dice:**\n   Since the rolls of the two dice are independent events, we multiply the probabilities of each event.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability of not rolling a prime number on both dice} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that Adam did not roll a prime number on either die is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\).<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nReview the solution above. Identify and correct any errors; if it is correct, retain its answer. Give your final answer inside \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n",
